  "privacyPolicyTitle": "Privacy policy",
  "privacyPolicyBody": "Updated October 21, 2026\n\nPhotos and face detection results are processed on your device and are not uploaded for processing. No account is required, and the app has no advertising SDK.\n\nCamera access is used to take photos. Photo library access is used to choose photos and save finished images, only when you use those features.\n\nSaved results are also stored in the app’s private album. Delete them in My Photos. Exported copies must be deleted separately in the system photo library. System photo syncing and backups follow your device settings. Language and custom specifications are stored locally.\n\nGoogle ML Kit performs face detection locally, but can send technical diagnostics and usage metrics to Google, including device/app information, per-installation identifiers, API events, performance and errors. These metrics do not include your input photos or detection results. ONNX Runtime runs the bundled background-removal model locally.\n\nAndroid checks GitHub for app updates and downloads updates on request. iOS updates come from the App Store. Opening the online policy uses your browser.\n\nQuestions: chunguangwee@gmail.com. The online policy provides further details and links to Google’s SDK disclosures.\n\nTemporary export copies are kept in the app cache so receiving apps can read them. Copies older than one day are removed at the next app launch or export.",
